    "collapsible_text_YPVYyd": {
      "type": "collapsible-text",
      "disabled": true,
      "settings": {
        "richtext": "<p>Rubber mats are a familiar and practical choice, especially in wet weather. EVA mats offer a different approach: a vehicle-specific shape and cellular structure designed to keep water and dirt in place. The best choice depends on fit, floor coverage, cleaning and how you use your vehicle.</p>",
        "collapsible_richtext": "<p><strong>Why are rubber mats popular?</strong><br/>Rubber does not absorb water, withstands everyday use well and is easy to rinse. However, the result depends on the quality and fit of the selected set. Water and dirt remain exposed on the surface, and a universal or poorly fitted mat can move or leave parts of the floor unprotected. The smell and flexibility also depend on the rubber compound and temperature.</p>",
        "button_text_more": "Read more",
        "button_text_less": "Show less",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 50,
        "padding_bottom": 57
      }
    },
    "image_with_collapsible_text_XCLeBp": {
      "type": "image-with-collapsible-text",
      "disabled": true,
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Frame_234.png",
        "header": "<h2>What should you <strong>check before choosing</strong> car mats?</h2>",
        "richtext": "<p>Start with the exact vehicle version. The mats should follow the floor contours, use the correct fastening points and remain safely clear of the pedals. Also compare floor coverage, material quality and how easily the set can be cleaned. Appearance matters, but safe fit and stability come first.</p>",
        "collapsible_richtext": "<h3>What types of rubber mats are available?</h3><p>The two most common designs are tray-style mats with a raised edge and standard-profile mats. A raised edge helps contain a larger amount of water or melting snow. Standard mats use channels or a textured surface to limit the movement of water and mud. In both cases, the mat must fit the vehicle and remain securely fixed.</p>",
        "button_text_more": "Read more",
        "button_text_less": "Show less",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 80,
        "padding_bottom": 80
      }
    },
    "text_with_image_zBPL3c": {
      "type": "text-with-image",
      "disabled": true,
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Rectangle_91_1.png",
        "header": "<p><strong>EVA or rubber?</strong> The key differences in everyday use</p>",
        "richtext": "<p>Both materials protect the vehicle floor from water and dirt without absorbing moisture. Rubber mats keep liquids on the open surface or in channels. EVA cells divide the surface into small compartments that limit the movement of water, sand and mud. Carvion EVA mats are also made for a specific vehicle, so they can protect more of the shaped floor while remaining lightweight and easy to remove.</p>",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 80,
        "padding_bottom": 80
      }
    },
    "richtext_section_K7WAxg": {
      "type": "richtext-section",
      "disabled": true,
      "settings": {
        "header": "<p>Why choose <strong>Carvion EVA mats?</strong></p>",
        "richtext": "<p>Each Carvion set is made to order for a specific vehicle using measured templates. The mats are cut, finished and quality-checked in Poland. You can choose the colour of the material and binding to create a set that suits both your vehicle and your style.</p>",
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
        "padding_top": 58,
        "padding_bottom": 57
      }
    },
